<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="recommended-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_paladin_shieldofthetemplar.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Recommended Gear for Protection Paladins in Mists of Pandaria Classic</span></h2>
<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="what-is-the-bis-protection-paladin-gear">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_helmet_plate_raidpaladin_l_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> What is the BiS Protection Paladin gear?</h3>
<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>Protection Paladins have a very clear identity when it comes to gearing, and their <a data-contiguous="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/guide/classes/paladin/protection/tank-stat-priority-pve">Stat Priorities</a> break away from the traditional tank mold. While most other tanks lean on avoidance and raw durability to stay alive, Paladins prioritize consistency, control, and tempo. We’re not trying to “get hit less”, we’re focused on never missing a beat in our active mitigation. That changes how we approach gear, often pushing us toward items that are typically sought after by DPS, even when gearing defensively.<br/>
<br/>This works because of the natural synergy between our stat priorities and how we function in combat. <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=84839/vengeance">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_charm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vengeance</span></a> gives us all the Attack Power we need, removing the pressure to stack Strength. That opens the door to focus on Hit, Expertise, and Haste, which not only boost our damage but also increase our survivability. They make our spells hit reliably, meaning our Holy Power generation speeds up and <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=53600/shield-of-the-righteous">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_shieldofvengeance.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shield of the Righteous</span></a> will be available when we need it most.<br/>
<br/>Staggered raid releases make gearing considerations even more nuanced. You'll often be forced to choose between a strong temporary upgrade now, or holding out for a less competitive piece later so it doesn't go to waste. But with tanks contributing meaningful damage, these aren’t just defensive decisions, they’re progression calls. Picking the right gear at the right time might be what pushes your group over the line. This guide reflects that mindset. The sets outlined here favor pieces that strike a balance between immediate strength and long-term planning. We’ll highlight less contested items in slots likely to be replaced, while leaning into powerful early options that justify the tradeoff. Whether you’re chasing early clears or laying a solid foundation for a relaxed progression, this approach ensures your gearing choices make sense, both for you and your raid.<ul class="exclude-units"></ul>
<br/>
<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="bis-gear">Overall Best in Slot Gear for Protection Paladins</h3>Raids releases in Phase 1 of Mists of Pandaria Classic will be staggered, with a few resets between each raid opening. This means that as the Phase progresses, more of your Best in Slot gear will become available to you. This also means that you will need to find alternatives until your Best in Slot items are available. The following gearsets are designed to guide you through early progression: The Phase 1 BiS set assumes full access and no loot restrictions. The Mogu'Shan Vault and Heart of Fear sets serve as realistic stepping stones until he next raid becomes available. These intermediate sets prioritize high-impact, long-lasting pieces where it matters, while filling other slots with alternatives that are less contested by DPS but still exceptionally effective progression picks.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
