<div class="exclude-units" id="tab-bis-lists-heart-of-fear" role="tabpanel" style="display: none;" tabindex="0">This list represents the best progression picks available up to and including <b>Heart of Fear</b> in Mists of Pandaria Classic Phase 1. An item to look out for specifically is <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86955/waistplate-of-overwhelming-assault">
<img alt="Waistplate of Overwhelming Assault" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_plate_raidwarrior_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Waistplate of Overwhelming Assault</span></a>, our best belt option byr far in Phase 1. <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86957/ring-of-the-bladed-tempest">
<img alt="Ring of the Bladed Tempest" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_epicring_a3.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ring of the Bladed Tempest</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86945/hiseks-chrysanthemum-cape">
<img alt="Hisek's Chrysanthemum Cape" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cape_pandaria_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Hisek's Chrysanthemum Cape</span></a> would be incredible pick-ups as they are rightfully in our Phase 1 BiS set, but ultimately not decisive enough to pick over DPS who have far fewer options. <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86979/impaling-treads">
<img alt="Impaling Treads" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_plate_raidwarrior_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Impaling Treads</span></a> is a good inclusion in many more aggressive sets you'd want to wear during farm, for progression content it is worth waiting on <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=90507/deepwater-greatboots">
<img alt="Deepwater Greatboots" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_plate_raiddeathknight_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Deepwater Greatboots</span></a> instead. Finally, let's quickly talk about weapons: <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=84839/vengeance">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_charm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vengeance</span></a> scaling AP means weapon base damage is devalued a lot compared to damage dealing classes. The PvP 4 Set is still potent; you should only consider breaking the set once you've acquired a full set of 509 Item Level items.<br/>
