<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="set-bonuses">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_chest_plate_raidpaladin_l_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Tier &amp; Set Bonuses for Protection Paladins in Mists of Pandaria Classic</span></h2>The Tier 14 Protection set is nothing to write home about, but good enough to still wear it over the alternatives at least during progression. A one minute CD reduction on <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=31850/ardent-defender">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_ardentdefender.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ardent Defender</span></a> is good, enhancing yet another tool in your already strong catalogue of CD options once you've acquired two set pieces. The four piece bonus sounds very strong at first glance, but ultimately ends up being a relatively small relative survivability increase when we were already extremely unlikely to perish, a typical "win more" scenario. When using <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=114163/eternal-flame">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_torch_thrown.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Eternal Flame</span></a>, the bonus becomes slightly more relevant. Finally, the set bonus reaches peak usefulness in encounters with very frequent damage spikes such as Sha of Fear.  That said, none of the alternatives are enticing enough to make us opt out of running it until the content is trivialised.<br/>
<br/>The Tier 14 Retribution set provides an interesting alternative once you feel reasonably confident in the content. The 2-Piece bonus is entirely irrelevant, the 4-Piece Bonus however is a slight offensive boost. While it does nothing for our seals since we are using Seal of Insight almost exclusively, it still increase our Judgment damage. However, this is not the reason to consider wearing the ret set: the stats are simply much more useful for us than what we would get wearing the Protection set. Specifically the amount of Haste available on the Retribution set makes it a very enticing option.<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="tier-14-tank">
