<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Protection Paladin</span></h2>In Mists of Pandaria your Hit cap is 7.5% Hit (or 2550 Hit Rating), whereas for Expertise the caps are split into 7.5% Expertise (or 2550 Expertise Rating) to reach the so-called "soft cap", and 15% Expertise (or 5100 Expertise Rating) to reach the true "hard cap". Keep in mind that some abilities such as the <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" data-contiguous="true" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/race_draenei_female.gif");'></span> Draenei Racial Heroic Presence will contribute to your overall Hit and/<wbr/>or Expertise needed.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="hit-rating">Hit Rating</h4>At 7.5% Hit, your melee hits can no longer miss Raid bosses. Spells, however, operate on a different Hit table and it would require additional investment into Hit to negate this miss chance entirely. In Mists of Pandaria, there exists another option: most tanks will now look to solve their Spell Hit woes through Expertise.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="expertise-rating">Expertise Rating</h4>At 7.5% Expertise, Raid bosses will no longer be able to Dodge your attack, but they can still Parry them. For most Raid encounters, you should aim to reach the full 15% Expertise cap to eliminate both Dodge and Parry from the equation. All gear sets recommended in this guide will meet this cap. There are exceptions, though: Some Raid bosses either cannot Parry due to encounter mechanics or positioning, and can therefore be dealt with in such a way that parries aren't a concern. In those cases, it may be wise to reforge or swap gear to favor other stats.<br/>
<br/>Additionally, reaching 7.5% Expertise will also make you achieve Spell Hit cap, ensuring your spells such as <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=26573/consecration">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_innerfire.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Consecration</span></a> won't miss.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_uncut_purple.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Gemming for Protection Paladin</span></h2>Reaching the Expertise hard cap remains a top priority, and while you initially often had to rely on <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76693/precise-primordial-ruby">
<img alt="Precise Primordial Ruby" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_red.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Precise Primordial Ruby</span></a> to get there, this becomes much less of an effort once you start acquiring gear in raids. Because of this, we can afford to shift more of our gems towards <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76699/quick-suns-radiance">
<img alt="Quick Sun's Radiance" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_yellow.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Quick Sun's Radiance</span></a>. However, it's usually worth aiming for socket bonuses that grant Expertise, Hit, Haste, or Stamina in roughly that order of priority. To meet those bonuses efficiently, make use of hybrid gems like <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76667/wicked-vermilion-onyx">
<img alt="Wicked Vermilion Onyx" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_orange.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Wicked Vermilion Onyx</span></a>, <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76681/accurate-imperial-amethyst">
<img alt="Accurate Imperial Amethyst" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_purple.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Accurate Imperial Amethyst</span></a> and <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76642/lightning-wild-jade">
<img alt="Lightning Wild Jade" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_green.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightning Wild Jade</span></a>. <br/>
<br/>On certain encounters with high spike damage, such as Grand Empress Shek'zeer or Sha of Fear you may want to consider swapping in more <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76639/solid-rivers-heart">
<img alt="Solid River's Heart" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_blue.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Solid River's Heart</span></a>  or <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76700/fractured-suns-radiance">
<img alt="Fractured Sun's Radiance" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_yellow.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fractured Sun's Radiance</span></a> to bolster your defenses. Finally, keep in mind <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76895/austere-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Austere Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_metagem_cut.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Austere Primal Diamond</span></a> will always stick around as a meta gem option to increase your survivability, although <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76886/reverberating-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Reverberating Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_metagem_cut.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reverberating Primal Diamond</span></a>  will likely be the most common option once you've geared up a bit.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
