<img alt="ad" src="//r2.rev.iq/wowhead.com/House_BlizzGear_Plushies_728x90.webp"/></a></div></div></div>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="engineering">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_engineering.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Engineering for Protection Paladins</h4>
<a data-contiguous="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/guide/professions/engineering/overview">Engineering</a> continues to be the dominant profession. <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=126731/synapse-springs">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Synapse Springs</span></a> provides a short, temporary, but entirely controllable burst and surivivability tool. That is admittedly not that enticing on its own, but you need to consider the full package: <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=55016/nitro-boosts">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nitro Boosts</span></a> provides one of the strongest movement speed boosts in the game, and <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=126392/goblin-glider">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Goblin Glider</span></a> replaces the old parachute with a steerable glide, letting you carry momentum and cover ground fast, in particular when going down slopes or stairs such as in Mogu'Shan Vault. As if that isn't enough to sell you on this profession on its own, Engineering also provides strong exclusive craftables in <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77539/reinforced-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Reinforced Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reinforced Retinal Armor</span></a> and <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77530/ghost-iron-dragonling">
<img alt="Ghost Iron Dragonling" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_head_dragon_bronze.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ghost Iron Dragonling</span></a>, with the former potentially lasting you up until all the way into the Heart of Fear. Oh, there's also a truckload of <a data-contiguous="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77589/g91-landshark">bombs</a>, <a data-contiguous="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=32413/frost-grenade">grenades</a>, <a data-contiguous="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=127132/wormhole-generator-pandaria">portals</a>, <a data-contiguous="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=49040/jeeves">butlers</a>, more <a data-contiguous="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=84411/high-powered-bolt-gun">bombs</a> and <a data-contiguous="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=40771/cobalt-frag-bomb#comments">grenades</a>, and other <a data-contiguous="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=56462/gnomish-army-knife">fun stuff</a> included in this profession. Easy pick.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="blacksmithing">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_blacksmithing.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Blacksmithing for Protection Paladins</h4>
<a data-contiguous="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/guide/professions/blacksmithing/overview">Blacksmithing</a> effectively provides you with two additional sockets. This is already enough to bring Blacksmithing in line with all the other professions, but where it stands out is versatility: these gems can be socketed with any stat you prefer. As tanks we already are very likely to favour secondary stats, which are more abundant on gems since Mists of Pandaria, meaning Blacksmithing effectively provides us with the equivalent of 640 secondary stats. Eventually, there will be epic gems too making this pick entirely future proof—but let's stick to the here and now.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="leatherworking">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_leatherworking.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Leatherworking for Protection Paladins</h4>
<a data-contiguous="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/guide/professions/leatherworking/overview">Leatherworking</a> continues to live on the fringes of ideal profession choices, providing a unique Bracers enchant in <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=124553/fur-lining-stamina">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_pelt_10.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fur Lining - Stamina</span></a>. The abscence of a basic Stamina enchant for bracers thereby makes Leatherworking effectively provide an extra 255 Stamina. However, the alternatives <a class="q1 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=74700/enchant-bracer-mastery">
<img alt="Enchant Bracer - Mastery" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_enchantedscroll.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Bracer - Mastery</span></a> and <a class="q1 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=74704/enchant-bracer-exceptional-strength">
<img alt="Enchant Bracer - Exceptional Strength" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_enchantedscroll.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Bracer - Exceptional Strength</span></a> are still good and we are generally not as Stamina-hungry as in previous expansions. You also get access to <a class="q2 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=29530/drums-of-speed">
<img alt="Drums of Speed" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_drum_04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Drums of Speed</span></a>, which offers a bit of encounter-specific utility when coordinated well. It won’t be immediately noticable, but it has its uses.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Crafted &amp; Profession Gear for Protection Paladin</span></h2>Crafted gear is no longer profession-locked for the most part, meaning even non-Blacksmiths can use Blacksmithing items. The main exceptions are <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77539/reinforced-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Reinforced Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reinforced Retinal Armor</span></a>, <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77530/ghost-iron-dragonling">
<img alt="Ghost Iron Dragonling" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_head_dragon_bronze.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ghost Iron Dragonling</span></a>  and <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=75274/zen-alchemist-stone">
<img alt="Zen Alchemist Stone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pet_scorchedstone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Zen Alchemist Stone</span></a> , which still requires respective profession skills to be equipped.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87406/gauntlets-of-battle-command">
<img alt="Gauntlets of Battle Command" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlets_plate_raiddeathknight_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gauntlets of Battle Command</span></a> — Solid option for defensive or hybrid setups. Slightly edges out <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87407/bloodforged-warfists">
<img alt="Bloodforged Warfists" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlet_plate_raidwarrior_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bloodforged Warfists</span></a> for survivability, but the difference is marginal.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87407/bloodforged-warfists">
<img alt="Bloodforged Warfists" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlet_plate_raidwarrior_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bloodforged Warfists</span></a> — Better pick for offensive and balanced sets. Worth running if you're already comfortable with survivability.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87402/ornate-battleplate-of-the-master">
<img alt="Ornate Battleplate of the Master" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_plate_raiddeathknight_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ornate Battleplate of the Master</span></a> — Mastery and Expertise make it a strong balanced piece. Edges out <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87405/unyielding-bloodplate">
<img alt="Unyielding Bloodplate" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_plate_raidwarrior_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unyielding Bloodplate</span></a> overall and can be worn until acquiring the heroic tier chest.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87405/unyielding-bloodplate">
<img alt="Unyielding Bloodplate" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_plate_raidwarrior_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unyielding Bloodplate</span></a> — Slightly more defensive than <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87402/ornate-battleplate-of-the-master">
<img alt="Ornate Battleplate of the Master" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_plate_raiddeathknight_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ornate Battleplate of the Master</span></a>, but not by a huge margin.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77539/reinforced-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Reinforced Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reinforced Retinal Armor</span></a> — Extremely strong early on thanks to customizable sockets. Loses some ground later but still hard to beat in terms of value, and will likely remain BiS in Challenge Modes.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=82979/breastplate-of-ancient-steel">
<img alt="Breastplate of Ancient Steel" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_plate_raidwarrior_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Breastplate of Ancient Steel</span></a> — Very solid stopgap if you can't afford crafted 496s or raid is yet to release. Edges out most dungeon options for raw mitigation.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=82980/gauntlets-of-ancient-steel">
<img alt="Gauntlets of Ancient Steel" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlet_plate_raidwarrior_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gauntlets of Ancient Steel</span></a> — Similar use case as <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=82979/breastplate-of-ancient-steel">
<img alt="Breastplate of Ancient Steel" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_plate_raidwarrior_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Breastplate of Ancient Steel</span></a>, but likely more affordable and can be acquired before Raids release.</div></li></ul>
